  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2503(b), the annual gift tax exclusion applies only to present interest gifts. Crummey withdrawal powers (Crummey v. Commissioner, 397 F.2d 82) convert contributions to an ILIT into present interests by giving each beneficiary a temporary right to withdraw. With 4 beneficiaries, the exclusion covers 4 x $19,000 = $76,000, and since the $40,000 premium is below $76,000, no taxable gift results.
